WEBVTT

00:45.045 --> 00:48.048
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

00:49.258 --> 00:50.259
Yes.

00:50.759 --> 00:52.344
From what I've gathered

00:52.427 --> 00:54.179
no one has noticed anything yet.

00:55.889 --> 00:58.225
There's no one left to make a scene

00:58.308 --> 01:01.228
so you should be able to
finalize this deal quietly.

01:02.688 --> 01:05.315
Oh, you're talking about
Cho Ye-rin, right?

01:06.316 --> 01:08.235
I had her sent away to the outpost

01:08.318 --> 01:09.945
so what can she possibly do from there?

01:10.737 --> 01:11.738
Then again

01:12.030 --> 01:13.448
if she really becomes a problem...

01:15.409 --> 01:16.827
should I just take care of her?

01:28.171 --> 01:29.965
Looks like we have a rat.

01:30.591 --> 01:32.134
I'll call you back.

01:42.352 --> 01:43.604
Who the hell is it?

01:43.687 --> 01:45.105
Show yourself!

02:26.938 --> 02:29.858
A new quest has arrived.

02:31.318 --> 02:34.905
Which of the following
is a fresh kudzu root?

02:34.988 --> 02:37.783
What? Damn it, how am I...

02:38.533 --> 02:40.827
supposed to know that?

02:41.453 --> 02:43.372
The Chef's Eye is being used.

02:44.873 --> 02:46.458
A fresh kudzu root

02:46.541 --> 02:49.878
is covered all over in brown fuzz

02:50.253 --> 02:51.880
and is not too thin and not too thick

02:51.963 --> 02:54.091
which is a decent size.

02:56.927 --> 02:57.928
Damn it.

03:02.391 --> 03:03.558
Correct.

03:03.642 --> 03:05.060
CORRECT!

03:16.655 --> 03:17.656
Kang Seong-jae!

03:20.033 --> 03:21.910
Grab my hand. Quick!

03:22.577 --> 03:23.578
Thank you.

03:25.580 --> 03:29.334
EPISODE 7

03:31.169 --> 03:32.379
Gosh, my arm hurts.

03:34.631 --> 03:36.341
What were you doing back there?

03:38.135 --> 03:41.179
- I'm sorry.
- No, I'm not trying to yell at you.

03:41.263 --> 03:43.640
But if you space out for even
a second in a place like this

03:43.724 --> 03:45.058
you could get hurt.

03:45.142 --> 03:47.352
What would you have done
if I wasn't here, huh?

03:54.067 --> 03:55.986
What are those guys doing over there?

04:02.242 --> 04:03.994
But are you sure this is really okay?

04:04.077 --> 04:07.164
Otherwise, we'd have to go
all the way down to the water truck.

04:07.247 --> 04:08.373
That would take forever.

04:08.457 --> 04:09.958
I know, but still.

04:10.041 --> 04:11.460
This water flows

04:11.543 --> 04:14.379
from the most pristine land
in the Republic of Korea.

04:14.463 --> 04:15.672
What's the problem?

04:15.756 --> 04:17.966
Besides, all the senior soldiers
did it this way.

04:18.967 --> 04:21.011
Hurry and fill it up.

04:22.137 --> 04:23.555
What are you doing over there?

04:34.399 --> 04:35.901
I said, what are you doing?

04:38.445 --> 04:39.946
Hey, you, Kang Seong-jae.

04:40.030 --> 04:42.157
Where have you been messing around, huh?

04:42.407 --> 04:44.493
What's with all the noise during training?

04:45.243 --> 04:47.788
I'm sorry. The fog was thick,
so I got lost.

04:48.288 --> 04:49.790
Outpost Commander, Master Sergeant.

04:49.873 --> 04:51.333
Aren't you looking after your men?

04:51.750 --> 04:53.460
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

04:53.543 --> 04:56.338
Kang Seong-jae. I keep telling you
you're great, and then you pull this.

04:56.421 --> 04:57.964
- I'm sorry.
- It's fine.

04:58.548 --> 04:59.591
As long as you're not hurt.

04:59.800 --> 05:00.801
Go on.

05:01.760 --> 05:02.803
Excuse me, Company Commander.

05:05.013 --> 05:06.473
There's something I must report to you.

05:07.516 --> 05:08.517
What is it?

05:08.975 --> 05:12.062
The opposing force
that infiltrated through this tunnel...

05:12.938 --> 05:15.440
was discovered by the 4th Company

05:15.524 --> 05:17.150
and they were wiped out.

05:17.234 --> 05:19.110
- Oh, really?
- Yes, sir.

05:19.402 --> 05:23.198
How did they find who'd tunneled?
Did they bring in dogs or something?

05:23.281 --> 05:24.658
I'm not sure myself...

05:24.825 --> 05:26.493
but they say
Private Kang Seong-jae found them.

05:26.701 --> 05:28.745
- That cook?
- Yes.

05:33.333 --> 05:35.418
- Salute!
- Salute.

05:35.502 --> 05:37.420
- Company Commander.
- Yes, Regimental Commander.

05:37.504 --> 05:38.713
I hear you took down
an opposing force platoon?

05:41.341 --> 05:43.718
- That's right, sir.
- How'd you find them? Explain.

05:43.802 --> 05:44.970
Yes, sir.

05:45.971 --> 05:49.391
Well, I just sensed something was off.

05:52.185 --> 05:55.605
So you just acted on a hunch?

05:58.108 --> 06:00.527
It's all thanks to you,
Regimental Commander.

06:00.610 --> 06:02.112
Oh, please.

06:03.488 --> 06:04.656
Goodness.

06:10.370 --> 06:11.997
Don't!

06:12.080 --> 06:13.790
You scared me! Oh, it's hot!

06:13.874 --> 06:15.458
What is it now? What?

06:15.542 --> 06:18.420
There's a problem with the drinking water.

06:22.048 --> 06:24.134
Anyone experiencing stomach pains

06:24.217 --> 06:25.760
step forward now.

06:25.844 --> 06:28.555
Because of these irresponsible punks

06:28.638 --> 06:30.640
the entire company
is going down the drain.

06:31.600 --> 06:33.268
Master Sergeant, it looks like
we're short two men.

06:33.560 --> 06:35.687
What? Did everyone turn in their canteens?

06:36.688 --> 06:37.814
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

06:37.898 --> 06:39.065
Then why are two missing?

06:39.149 --> 06:40.233
Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.

06:40.317 --> 06:43.069
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol and Private First
Class Pyo Ji-yong are missing.

06:43.153 --> 06:44.362
Gosh.

06:45.572 --> 06:47.324
We eat this Korean
military-style bag ramyun

06:47.407 --> 06:49.451
but why am I happy to see it here?

06:49.534 --> 06:52.829
I swiped it from the cooks'
snack box, sir.

06:52.913 --> 06:54.539
Give me some if you get more food.

06:54.623 --> 06:55.957
I got it, punk.

06:56.750 --> 06:58.793
But this water's a bit lukewarm, isn't it?

06:58.877 --> 07:01.504
I barely found where the Medical Unit
hid their hot water container.

07:01.713 --> 07:03.381
I guess it is a little lukewarm, sir.

07:04.382 --> 07:06.134
Gosh, why does this water taste so weird?

07:06.217 --> 07:07.260
It tastes fishy.

07:08.637 --> 07:10.639
Damn it. Did those punks
just scoop this up from anywhere?

07:10.722 --> 07:12.891
Don't you like your noodles
on the firm side anyway?

07:13.308 --> 07:14.309
Right.

07:15.101 --> 07:16.144
Cheers?

07:16.227 --> 07:17.228
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

07:18.063 --> 07:20.065
Gosh... a smoke after a meal.

07:20.148 --> 07:21.232
Now this is the life.

07:21.316 --> 07:22.651
I feel alive again.

07:23.109 --> 07:25.070
I was wondering
what kind of crazy bastards

07:25.153 --> 07:28.323
would be smoking during a drill,
and it was you guys, huh?

07:28.406 --> 07:29.741
Master Sergeant,
it's not what it looks like.

07:30.283 --> 07:31.534
We just picked up
what someone else threw away.

07:31.952 --> 07:35.038
I see you enjoyed a meal
with Korean military-style bag ramyun.

07:35.121 --> 07:36.247
Kim Kwan-cheol.

07:36.331 --> 07:38.375
- Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.
- Do you think this drill is a joke?

07:39.584 --> 07:41.753
- Pyo Ji-yong.
- Private First Class Pyo Ji-yong.

07:41.836 --> 07:44.130
You think this is a camping trip?
Follow me.

07:45.840 --> 07:47.300
Follow me, you punk...

07:48.051 --> 07:51.221
- Hey. Stop whining and follow me.
- Sir, just a second...

07:52.514 --> 07:54.349
What's this? What's that smell?

07:56.393 --> 07:57.769
- Attention!
- No...

07:57.852 --> 07:59.396
- Snap out of it! Attention!
- Please, help me!

07:59.479 --> 08:00.480
You...

08:01.982 --> 08:03.108
What the...

08:04.901 --> 08:08.488
Wait. What water
did you use for the ramyun?

08:08.571 --> 08:09.698
The... The Medical Unit.

08:09.781 --> 08:11.616
You cooked it with that water?

08:11.700 --> 08:13.076
You damn idiot!

08:13.743 --> 08:14.828
Now...

08:31.052 --> 08:32.971
Man, that stench is killer.

08:36.599 --> 08:39.936
Don't you know securing water
is as important as food in combat?

08:40.020 --> 08:42.397
And you call yourselves medics?
Is this some kind of joke?

08:43.648 --> 08:45.942
We threw out that spicy chicken stew
for nothing.

08:46.026 --> 08:48.111
- Make sure bastards are disciplined.
- Yes, sir.

08:48.194 --> 08:49.279
Support Section Chief.

08:49.946 --> 08:52.615
Support Section Chief,
you didn't confirm the cause

08:52.699 --> 08:54.576
and just reported that
the cooks were the problem?

08:55.827 --> 08:57.037
Well...

08:57.120 --> 08:58.663
since they were cooking outdoors

08:58.747 --> 09:01.124
I figured we couldn't rule out
it could have easily spoiled...

09:01.207 --> 09:03.460
Are soldiers supposed to file reports
based on speculation?

09:04.127 --> 09:05.128
I apologize.

09:05.962 --> 09:07.672
Since everyone just passes the buck

09:07.756 --> 09:09.382
this is why we have no unit cohesion!

09:10.383 --> 09:11.468
I'm sorry, Regimental Commander.

09:13.762 --> 09:15.180
Let's sort out issues

09:15.263 --> 09:17.348
and see this through to the end properly.

09:17.932 --> 09:18.975
Got it?

09:19.309 --> 09:20.351
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

09:20.685 --> 09:23.104
You made a play. Why the long face?

09:23.188 --> 09:24.439
Oh, it's nothing, sir.

09:28.234 --> 09:30.820
Oh, you're talking about
Cho Ye-rin, right?

09:34.908 --> 09:36.534
Should I just take care of her?

09:47.253 --> 09:49.798
We'll begin the KCTC After-Action Review.

09:50.090 --> 09:53.051
Our 60th Regiment seemed to be
on the back foot initially

09:53.384 --> 09:57.180
but by wiping out the Viper Unit
through tunnels, the win probability

09:57.597 --> 10:00.433
rose from 15.4% to over 50%.

10:00.517 --> 10:02.727
This is an unprecedented achievement

10:02.811 --> 10:04.854
in the Korean Combat Training Center.

10:04.938 --> 10:08.274
- For discovering the Viper Unit...
- Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun!

10:08.358 --> 10:09.901
- And for wiping out the tunnel team...
- Private Kang Seong-jae!

10:09.984 --> 10:12.529
We'll now present the War Hero award

10:12.612 --> 10:15.532
to Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun
and Private Kang Seong-jae.

10:15.615 --> 10:17.784
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun! Thank you!

10:17.867 --> 10:19.369
29TH DIVISION KCTC TRAINING
OUTSTANDING UNIT AWARD CEREMONY

10:19.452 --> 10:20.787
Private Kang Seong-jae!

10:20.870 --> 10:23.498
In my years, I've never seen this.

10:23.581 --> 10:25.416
A private as a war hero

10:25.500 --> 10:27.502
and a cook, no less.

10:27.585 --> 10:29.462
I'll be keeping an eye on you.

10:29.546 --> 10:30.964
Private Kang Seong-jae!

10:31.047 --> 10:32.674
It's an honor to be standing here.

10:32.757 --> 10:34.759
Sergeant Yoon and Private Kang

10:34.843 --> 10:36.678
will be awarded a five-day leave.

10:36.761 --> 10:39.973
An award will be presented to the company
that showed outstanding performance.

10:40.056 --> 10:42.892
Captain Hwang Seok-ho, commander
of the 4th Company, come forward.

10:44.602 --> 10:46.646
Captain Hwang Seok-ho!

10:48.898 --> 10:51.901
I can't believe a day like this
has come for me, Hwang Seok-ho.

10:52.485 --> 10:55.029
I wasn't expecting this,
so I didn't prepare a speech.

10:58.199 --> 10:59.784
Well, first of all...

10:59.868 --> 11:02.453
An army marches on its stomach.

11:02.537 --> 11:03.788
Quest complete.

11:03.872 --> 11:07.250
You have gained
Experience Points and leveled up.

11:08.585 --> 11:11.254
A new feature, Colleague,
has been unlocked.

11:11.337 --> 11:12.547
Salute!

11:15.383 --> 11:17.135
29TH DIVISION KCTC TRAINING
OUTSTANDING UNIT AWARD CEREMONY

11:31.858 --> 11:32.859
Salute!

11:34.611 --> 11:36.863
I was worried
if you'd even be able to adjust

11:37.238 --> 11:39.032
but you show up and sweep all the awards.

11:40.033 --> 11:41.576
No, sir. I'll work even harder.

11:42.493 --> 11:43.912
Nothing wrong with working hard.

11:43.995 --> 11:44.996
But...

11:45.288 --> 11:46.623
how hard were you working

11:47.040 --> 11:48.416
to be dropping things like this?

12:12.941 --> 12:14.192
Our dear War Hero.

12:14.776 --> 12:16.694
What were you in such a hurry for...

12:16.778 --> 12:18.696
running off like you were escaping?

12:28.289 --> 12:29.999
You've still got a long way
to go in your service

12:30.166 --> 12:31.876
so if you get curious about anything,
feel free to ask.

12:32.502 --> 12:34.045
Don't just keep it to yourself.

12:39.133 --> 12:40.134
Seong-jae.

12:43.554 --> 12:44.555
Is something wrong?

12:46.724 --> 12:47.725
It's nothing.

12:48.935 --> 12:49.936
Okay, then.

12:50.019 --> 12:51.187
Let's head back.

12:51.688 --> 12:52.772
Yes, ma'am.

13:00.321 --> 13:02.198
GANGLIM

13:02.282 --> 13:04.701
- Salute!
- Salute!

13:05.743 --> 13:08.913
Private Kang Seong-jae.
Promoted to Private First Class.

13:08.997 --> 13:11.374
Reporting as ordered. Salute!

13:11.457 --> 13:12.709
Salute!

13:13.960 --> 13:15.503
So, how does it feel to be promoted?

13:16.713 --> 13:19.924
I'll approach with a greater sense
of responsibility, sir.

13:20.341 --> 13:24.595
And you know, you only achieved this

13:25.179 --> 13:26.431
because of an excellent commander.

13:26.597 --> 13:27.807
Yes, sir. I'm well aware.

13:29.642 --> 13:32.520
As long as you keep listening to me,
Hwang Seok-ho

13:32.603 --> 13:33.896
the rest of your military service...

13:34.731 --> 13:35.898
will go smoothly.

13:35.982 --> 13:37.275
Congratulations.

13:37.358 --> 13:39.777
Smile Badge has been cleared.

13:40.611 --> 13:43.865
You can now change your class
to Intermediate Cook.

13:43.948 --> 13:46.200
INTERMEDIATE COOK
CLASS CHANGE POSSIBLE

13:46.284 --> 13:47.744
Kang Seong-jae.

13:48.036 --> 13:49.245
Are you okay?

13:49.329 --> 13:50.455
Private Kang...

13:50.872 --> 13:51.873
Right.

13:53.750 --> 13:56.210
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.
I'm doing great, sir.

13:59.630 --> 14:01.341
GIYOUNG'S CHARCOAL-GRILLED CHICKEN

14:05.636 --> 14:07.513
- Is everyone here?
- Yes, sir.

14:07.597 --> 14:09.265
You all did a good job

14:09.349 --> 14:10.975
working your tails off in training.

14:11.059 --> 14:12.769
It's chicken!

14:14.771 --> 14:16.064
All right, listen up!

14:17.440 --> 14:19.734
And who am I?
The one and only Park Jae-young.

14:20.068 --> 14:21.819
My younger brother opened
a chicken restaurant.

14:27.617 --> 14:29.243
Hold on. Before you dig in

14:29.327 --> 14:30.828
I want your thoughts on the chicken.

14:30.912 --> 14:32.288
Joo Sang-uk, you're up!

14:34.874 --> 14:36.542
That charcoal aroma is perfect, sir.

14:36.626 --> 14:40.171
This looks way too good to taste bad.
Pass the chopsticks.

14:40.254 --> 14:41.297
Hold on. You're going on leave.

14:41.381 --> 14:43.841
Shouldn't you be full already?

14:43.925 --> 14:46.302
Hey, don't be like that, sir.
Okay, okay. Let's dig in.

14:46.386 --> 14:48.262
Thanks for the food!

14:48.346 --> 14:49.972
Enjoy the food, and make sure
you clean up properly.

14:51.766 --> 14:52.934
This is delicious.

14:53.017 --> 14:54.519
It's so good.

14:57.355 --> 14:58.356
My gosh.

14:58.773 --> 14:59.857
Hey, Kang Seong-jae.

15:00.733 --> 15:03.861
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.
- How's it taste, our Outpost Ace?

15:05.279 --> 15:07.156
These are noodles made from pork rind

15:07.573 --> 15:09.409
and they go really well
with the chicken, sir.

15:09.492 --> 15:12.078
See? That's the kind of answer
I'm talking about! See?

15:12.161 --> 15:14.455
Did you see that? He's analyzing
the ingredients even now.

15:14.539 --> 15:17.291
Our youngest is relentless, okay?

15:18.584 --> 15:20.002
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
you seem to be in a good mood.

15:20.086 --> 15:21.754
How could he not be?

15:21.838 --> 15:23.965
He's finally going on the leave
he's dying for.

15:24.048 --> 15:25.883
There's no turning back this time.

15:25.967 --> 15:27.343
I don't care if Kang Seong-jae collapses.

15:27.427 --> 15:28.886
I'm taking my leave.

15:28.970 --> 15:30.096
Okay, I get it.

15:30.179 --> 15:31.472
Just hurry up and eat, all right?

15:31.556 --> 15:34.809
I've assigned a Kitchen Assistant
to make sure you're taken care of.

15:35.685 --> 15:36.811
This is really the kicker...

15:37.687 --> 15:38.688
What is it?

15:40.064 --> 15:41.649
We came in to take a short break.

15:43.025 --> 15:45.987
What? What have you done
to already be taking a break? Huh?

15:46.821 --> 15:48.531
If it were up to me,
I'd send you to disciplinary training

15:48.614 --> 15:49.866
and make you run drills

15:49.949 --> 15:51.742
until you snapped out of it,
that wouldn't be enough.

15:51.826 --> 15:55.121
While everyone else was working hard,
you two snuck off on your own.

15:55.204 --> 15:57.915
You must've had a great time smoking
and eating military-style bag ramyun?

15:57.999 --> 15:59.375
You can't do that.

15:59.959 --> 16:04.255
You can't sneak off to smoke
and eat during training!

16:05.756 --> 16:07.175
All right, attention!

16:09.260 --> 16:10.636
- Attention.
- About-face!

16:11.137 --> 16:12.263
About-face.

16:12.346 --> 16:14.182
Make sure you finish the weeding.

16:14.265 --> 16:15.266
Go.

16:16.809 --> 16:18.769
All right, let's get to it!

16:18.853 --> 16:20.980
- Let's get to it!
- Let's get to it!

16:22.607 --> 16:24.358
This fried part is really...

16:25.401 --> 16:26.402
Damn it.

16:28.488 --> 16:30.573
Aren't they going too far?

16:31.032 --> 16:33.409
Anyone would think
only Barracks 1 did any training.

16:37.038 --> 16:40.249
Let's see if guys in Barracks 1 can laugh
when Yoon Dong-hyun leaves.

16:42.502 --> 16:43.503
Damn it.

16:54.055 --> 16:56.307
- It's fine. Carry on.
- Thank you.

16:59.018 --> 17:00.978
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
you're up already?

17:01.062 --> 17:03.064
I've been getting up
at the same time every day

17:03.147 --> 17:05.107
so my eyes just pop open.

17:05.358 --> 17:08.694
I'm restless thinking about
going on leave for the first time.

17:09.695 --> 17:12.240
Didn't you come to keep an eye on me
in case I collapse again?

17:12.532 --> 17:14.867
You've gotten much better
at reading people, haven't you?

17:16.035 --> 17:17.161
So, you think

17:17.245 --> 17:18.829
you can handle all this by yourself?

17:20.039 --> 17:21.624
Yes. I think I can handle it on my own.

17:21.707 --> 17:23.709
Right, you do a good job
on your own anyway.

17:23.793 --> 17:26.212
It's just a distraction
if some weirdos come to "help."

17:27.755 --> 17:30.341
Isn't your leave delayed because of me?

17:31.133 --> 17:32.552
No. Thanks to you

17:32.635 --> 17:33.928
I even got a reward

17:34.136 --> 17:36.222
so I get to take a longer leave.

17:39.225 --> 17:40.226
Thanks.

17:40.434 --> 17:41.435
Thank you.

17:47.858 --> 17:49.277
It's a little hot. Gosh, it's hot.

17:49.777 --> 17:51.237
LIKEABILITY

17:55.408 --> 17:57.910
A colleague has been added.

17:57.994 --> 18:00.204
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun.

18:03.332 --> 18:04.333
Have a good time on your leave.

18:04.417 --> 18:06.919
There's not much to help you with.

18:07.003 --> 18:08.296
You're good on your own.

18:09.046 --> 18:12.008
But Kim Kwan-cheol worries me.

18:12.091 --> 18:13.384
He's a real tyrant

18:13.467 --> 18:15.928
and when I'm gone,
he'll think he owns the place.

18:17.680 --> 18:19.348
Yes, I'll be careful
not to get on his bad side.

18:19.432 --> 18:21.517
You've got to be really careful. Got it?

18:22.560 --> 18:23.978
- I'm off.
- New skill

18:24.061 --> 18:26.897
"Comrade, help me" is now available.

18:27.273 --> 18:29.108
You can receive random help

18:29.191 --> 18:30.443
- from a registered comrade.
- Oh, I'll just

18:30.526 --> 18:31.902
clean this up before I go.

18:35.364 --> 18:36.657
Before I head out...

18:37.908 --> 18:40.161
I'll just help with serving the rice
and then I'll go.

18:40.953 --> 18:43.039
Man, it feels weird not doing this.
Really weird.

18:43.122 --> 18:44.707
Look at this. There's too much water.

18:46.125 --> 18:47.126
Thank you.

18:48.085 --> 18:50.338
YEONJU TERMINAL

18:50.755 --> 18:52.214
Just stepping outside for a bit

18:52.298 --> 18:53.924
look how much fresher the air is.

18:54.508 --> 18:55.926
Gosh, it feels so good.

19:00.097 --> 19:02.224
But why did I end up
making breakfast before I left?

19:03.267 --> 19:04.310
That's weird.

19:48.896 --> 19:52.149
Maybe without Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun
watching over me

19:52.858 --> 19:55.611
it seems to have turned out
better than usual.

20:26.350 --> 20:28.310
A Class Change Quest has arrived.

20:28.394 --> 20:29.687
INTERMEDIATE COOK CLASS CHANGE QUEST

20:29.770 --> 20:30.771
Round One.

20:30.855 --> 20:33.899
Survive the reign of Kim Kwan-cheol.

20:36.694 --> 20:39.447
The soldier with the worst affinity...

20:39.947 --> 20:42.199
must be made into a colleague.

20:45.244 --> 20:48.831
A frown that seems to carry
all the world's frustrations.

20:48.914 --> 20:51.333
Slanted eyes reminiscent of a snake.

20:51.417 --> 20:52.835
Chapped lips

20:53.294 --> 20:55.045
and even a thuggish swagger.

21:01.427 --> 21:02.803
This man is truly...

21:04.555 --> 21:06.140
the epitome of a troublemaker.

21:08.976 --> 21:10.603
Hey, Kang Seong-jae!

21:11.562 --> 21:14.440
- Yoon Dong-hyun's gone, stuck?
- Oh, no, sir.

21:14.857 --> 21:16.442
What's this? Spicy stir-fried pork?

21:16.525 --> 21:17.735
Yes, sir.

21:18.819 --> 21:19.987
Would you like to have a taste?

21:20.070 --> 21:21.781
No, I need to go on a diet.

21:21.864 --> 21:23.240
I've been eating too much.

21:24.658 --> 21:26.577
Joo Sang-uk's busy

21:26.660 --> 21:29.497
so I was wondering
who to assign as a Kitchen Assistant.

21:29.580 --> 21:32.708
And get this, Kim Kwan-cheol
actually volunteered to help.

21:35.294 --> 21:37.671
- Sir, I must have misheard you.
- Hey, Kim Kwan-cheol.

21:37.755 --> 21:38.756
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol!

21:38.839 --> 21:41.383
If I catch you bullshitting
because you're working with your junior

21:41.467 --> 21:42.927
you're out that very day. Got it?

21:43.010 --> 21:44.345
Don't you worry, sir.

21:44.428 --> 21:47.556
I'm better than Yoon Dong-hyun,
who can't season the food right.

21:47.640 --> 21:51.560
You sure have a smart mouth.
I'll shut it permanently.

21:52.645 --> 21:54.438
Anyway, with our Outpost Ace

21:54.522 --> 21:57.024
figure it out and make it clean and smart.

21:58.108 --> 21:59.235
You know what that means?

21:59.318 --> 22:01.695
- Who doesn't know what that means?
- What's it mean?

22:01.821 --> 22:03.614
Figure out, do it well, be smart.

22:03.697 --> 22:05.407
Well, look at you. Such a modern guy.

22:06.075 --> 22:08.369
Anyway, just do that "figure it out
and make it clean and smart" thing

22:08.452 --> 22:10.788
and, you know, do the thing. Got it?

22:10.871 --> 22:14.458
Yes, sir. I'll trust Outpost Ace,
Kang Seong-jae, and do my best.

22:14.542 --> 22:15.876
Figure it out and make it clean
and smart. You punk.

22:15.960 --> 22:17.795
Figure it out and make it clean
and smart! Salute!

22:19.255 --> 22:20.965
Gosh, he talks too much.

22:41.151 --> 22:42.820
- Ace.
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

22:43.612 --> 22:44.613
So you're the ace?

22:45.948 --> 22:48.450
- No, sir, that's not me.
- Why?

22:49.118 --> 22:50.286
Are you unhappy that I'm here?

22:50.744 --> 22:51.745
Your face right now...

22:52.288 --> 22:53.831
doesn't look too happy to see me.

22:57.126 --> 22:58.377
I can take a break, right?

22:59.378 --> 23:00.421
Besides...

23:00.504 --> 23:03.299
even if I don't help,
you'll manage on your own.

23:03.382 --> 23:04.383
Since you're the ace.

23:06.218 --> 23:07.803
Call me if Master Sergeant shows up.

23:07.887 --> 23:09.263
Yes, sir.

23:15.936 --> 23:17.521
You went on a trip again?

23:17.605 --> 23:19.899
But your only son is home on leave!

23:19.982 --> 23:23.444
Does that mean
we have to roll out the red carpet?

23:23.527 --> 23:24.904
Honey, hurry up.

23:24.987 --> 23:26.572
There are side dishes in the fridge

23:26.655 --> 23:27.990
so eat something if you're hungry.

23:28.073 --> 23:30.576
But I can't eat by myself... Hello?

23:34.371 --> 23:36.540
At this rate, I wonder if
I'm going to get a younger sibling.

23:44.423 --> 23:47.217
- Get over here!
- Coming through.

23:47.635 --> 23:49.178
Coming through.

23:49.261 --> 23:52.097
Oh, thank you, sir.
Wow, the rice is perfectly firm.

23:52.181 --> 23:53.515
I'll eat well, thank you.

23:55.351 --> 23:57.645
Ji-yong, you need to eat up
and grow big and strong.

23:58.145 --> 23:59.855
Loving juniors is loving the nation.

23:59.939 --> 24:01.649
You're the best, Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

24:01.732 --> 24:02.733
Let me know if you need more.

24:02.816 --> 24:04.818
It's unlimited refills for you.

24:04.902 --> 24:06.070
Thank you, sir.

24:06.153 --> 24:10.282
Corporal, if you give out that much,
there won't be enough for the people.

24:10.366 --> 24:11.784
- If it's not enough...
- Can I have another serving?

24:11.867 --> 24:12.993
Then just give them less.

24:13.535 --> 24:14.536
I can't even do this much?

24:18.374 --> 24:19.375
I'll enjoy the meal.

24:19.458 --> 24:20.626
Thank you.

24:20.709 --> 24:21.794
I love you, sir!

24:21.877 --> 24:24.129
Corporal Joo Sang-uk!

24:29.551 --> 24:31.053
- About rice noodles the other day...
- Get lost.

24:31.804 --> 24:32.805
Jeez.

24:33.931 --> 24:35.557
- Private First Class Tak Mun-ik.
- Yeah.

24:37.851 --> 24:39.603
Come on, sir.
Playing favorites is going too far.

24:39.687 --> 24:41.188
If you've got a problem with it,
come find me in Barracks 2.

24:42.231 --> 24:43.232
Savor it.

24:43.315 --> 24:45.067
It's a precious gift from your senior.

24:48.028 --> 24:49.071
Thank you, sir.

24:49.571 --> 24:50.614
I'm trying to bulk up.

24:50.698 --> 24:52.074
"Bulking up," my foot.

24:52.908 --> 24:55.577
So it begins...
the reign of Kim Kwan-cheol.

25:08.716 --> 25:10.300
Salute!

25:11.635 --> 25:12.636
Let's go.

25:17.516 --> 25:19.184
- Hey, Kang Seong-jae.
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

25:19.268 --> 25:20.310
We've got pork belly, right?

25:20.644 --> 25:22.312
Yes, sir. The pork
is thawing in the refrigerator

25:22.396 --> 25:23.856
to make stir-fried pork belly
with bean sprouts

25:23.939 --> 25:27.067
Stir-fried pork belly
with bean sprouts... Not feeling it.

25:27.151 --> 25:28.902
Pork belly's best grilled.

25:28.986 --> 25:29.987
That sounds excellent.

25:33.365 --> 25:34.533
NAMPYO DISTRIBUTION
HEALTHY KOREAN PORK

25:37.828 --> 25:38.996
What?

25:39.079 --> 25:40.414
Do I have to light the grill myself?

25:40.497 --> 25:43.417
Oh, I thought you were telling
Kang Seong-jae to do it.

25:44.418 --> 25:46.086
Oh, that's right.

25:46.670 --> 25:49.214
You were amazing
at grilling meat last time.

25:49.298 --> 25:51.300
Hey, Cinderella. Enough with the cleaning.

25:51.383 --> 25:52.676
Get over here and grill some meat for us.

25:53.302 --> 25:55.554
But we need this for meal service.
If you cook it now...

25:55.637 --> 25:57.723
What? Scared you'll get yelled at
by the Master Sergeant?

25:58.599 --> 26:01.018
Since when has the Master Sergeant
given a damn about the mess hall?

26:01.602 --> 26:03.228
But I really don't think
this is a good idea.

26:07.775 --> 26:08.776
What about it?

26:13.947 --> 26:15.407
We'll get in serious trouble for this.

26:15.491 --> 26:16.492
Why?

26:16.742 --> 26:17.743
Are you gonna snitch?

26:18.786 --> 26:20.662
Sure, write it up in one of those
anonymous complaint forms.

26:20.746 --> 26:21.955
How long has it been
since anyone checked that box?

26:22.039 --> 26:23.290
According to TMI

26:23.373 --> 26:25.459
he lost the key somewhere.

26:25.542 --> 26:26.710
Oops. What a shame.

26:35.552 --> 26:37.387
Let me ask you something,
because I'm genuinely curious.

26:37.471 --> 26:39.723
What's with that look in your eyes?

26:40.057 --> 26:42.476
Because everyone's fawning over you

26:42.559 --> 26:43.811
you think you own the place, don't you?

26:55.948 --> 26:58.158
- No, sir.
- We're going to enjoy food and go

26:58.492 --> 26:59.743
so you just do your job.

27:20.347 --> 27:21.515
Do you think...

27:21.598 --> 27:23.308
he'll tell Master Sergeant?

27:23.392 --> 27:24.434
Let him.

27:24.726 --> 27:25.936
What's he gonna do about it?

27:28.147 --> 27:29.731
- Set it up.
- Set it up.

27:29.815 --> 27:30.816
Yes, sir.

27:44.913 --> 27:47.666
Surviving the reign of Kim Kwan-cheol.

27:47.749 --> 27:49.084
INTERMEDIATE COOK CLASS CHANGE QUEST

27:49.168 --> 27:53.172
Make Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol
an ally within seven days

27:53.547 --> 27:56.675
and maintain Mess Hall Satisfaction Rating
at 50 or above.

27:58.135 --> 27:59.178
Failure to do so...

27:59.678 --> 28:02.181
will terminate The Chef's Path.

28:08.270 --> 28:09.646
I've sorted everything out.

28:10.063 --> 28:11.607
You should be able to proceed as planned.

28:12.566 --> 28:14.818
Let's handle this cleanly.
No problems, no talk.

28:15.402 --> 28:17.779
You can't afford any trouble
with your promotion coming up.

28:17.863 --> 28:18.906
Don't worry, sir.

28:20.490 --> 28:21.867
Keep a close eye on Cho Ye-rin.

28:23.452 --> 28:24.786
I'll make sure nothing goes wrong.

28:25.370 --> 28:26.371
Good.

28:31.001 --> 28:33.545
CLIENT REPRESENTATIVE: LEE MIN-GU
VENDOR REPRESENTATIVE: JUNG HUI-YEONG

28:33.629 --> 28:36.089
VENDOR PHONE: 010-0028-5900

28:38.550 --> 28:39.718
Nampyo...

28:40.969 --> 28:42.095
CLIENT REPRESENTATIVE: LEE MIN-GU
VENDOR REPRESENTATIVE: JUNG HUI-YEONG

28:42.179 --> 28:43.472
VENDOR PHONE: 010-0028-5900

28:45.015 --> 28:46.308
VENDOR PHONE: 010-0028-5900

28:52.773 --> 28:53.899
What?

28:53.982 --> 28:55.859
Hey, Mun-ik. Were we supposed to have
fried rice today?

28:56.276 --> 28:58.737
Isn't it because those guys from
the Barracks 2 had a barbecue?

28:59.238 --> 29:00.489
With Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun gone

29:00.572 --> 29:02.282
they're treating the mess hall
like their own fridge.

29:02.866 --> 29:05.744
Man, why is Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun's
leave so long?

29:05.994 --> 29:08.330
Damn it. I like meat too, you know.

29:08.413 --> 29:11.792
I'm considering switching sides,
even if it's just for a week.

29:11.875 --> 29:12.876
What was that?

29:24.930 --> 29:27.349
No, I got it.

29:27.432 --> 29:30.852
Current Mess Hall
Satisfaction Rating is 53.

29:31.436 --> 29:34.314
Maintain a rating of 50 or higher.

29:36.024 --> 29:39.069
Eat up. We've had plenty.

29:40.362 --> 29:41.905
Hey, Sang-won.

29:41.989 --> 29:44.825
A shot of soju with fish cake soup
after so long...

29:46.868 --> 29:47.995
You're not Sang-won?

29:48.078 --> 29:49.079
Who are...

29:49.162 --> 29:50.664
Oh, sorry.

30:19.526 --> 30:20.527
FISH-SHAPED ICE CREAM SANDWICH

30:24.364 --> 30:25.574
What are you looking at?

30:27.075 --> 30:28.118
Nothing, sir.

30:44.468 --> 30:46.845
I didn't realize the void
left by Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun...

30:46.928 --> 30:49.139
would be this big.

31:00.609 --> 31:02.986
I wonder if the outpost
is running without me.

31:05.572 --> 31:09.785
KANG SEONG-JAE

31:11.578 --> 31:13.538
Snap out of it! Are you crazy?

31:13.622 --> 31:15.999
Why are you on leave
worrying about the unit?

31:16.333 --> 31:18.085
Come on, Dong-hyun, get a grip.

31:21.254 --> 31:22.506
Thanks for your hard work.

31:25.133 --> 31:27.594
You look even more tired than when
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun was here.

31:28.512 --> 31:29.554
I'm fine, sir.

31:30.764 --> 31:32.349
Jeez, those Barracks 2 guys.

31:33.266 --> 31:35.352
The mood at the outpost is the worst,
thanks to Kim Kwan-cheol.

31:35.602 --> 31:38.146
Honestly, the only reason
we had it so easy

31:38.230 --> 31:40.107
was all thanks to Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun,
wasn't it?

31:40.190 --> 31:42.609
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun said
he wasn't this bad.

31:42.692 --> 31:44.569
That's what the Master Sergeant
told me too.

31:45.195 --> 31:47.781
I wonder what happened
to make him change so much.

31:48.031 --> 31:50.325
"Happen"? He was probably
always like that.

31:50.909 --> 31:53.578
It would've been a nightmare
if he'd stayed in the mess hall.

31:55.330 --> 31:58.375
Was Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol
originally assigned to the mess hall?

31:59.000 --> 32:00.168
This was before I got to the outpost

32:00.252 --> 32:02.045
but he was transferred from the mess hall.

32:02.462 --> 32:03.463
Yeah?

32:15.684 --> 32:17.185
344 ONGSEON-RO

32:21.064 --> 32:22.274
MANSANUP COMPRESSION PROCESSING INC

32:32.284 --> 32:33.285
Excuse me.

32:34.619 --> 32:36.913
- Yes? What is it?
- I need to ask you a question.

32:37.247 --> 32:39.791
Isn't this Nampyo Distribution?

32:40.041 --> 32:41.209
What distribution?

32:41.501 --> 32:43.503
Can't you tell by looking?
This is a junkyard.

32:58.143 --> 32:59.603
It seems there has been a mistake.

33:00.520 --> 33:02.063
Please don't worry.

33:02.147 --> 33:04.691
I will handle it without any problems.

33:05.609 --> 33:06.610
Yes.

33:13.783 --> 33:16.495
Cho Ye-rin. I can't just let this go.

33:24.836 --> 33:26.213
What's this?

33:26.546 --> 33:28.381
- Is it bread today?
- Yes, sir.

33:29.049 --> 33:31.384
Shall I grill a patty for you now, sir?

33:31.468 --> 33:34.846
After you're done eating,
I'd appreciate it if you could help.

33:34.930 --> 33:36.097
Why should I?

33:36.932 --> 33:38.141
You can do everything yourself.

33:38.225 --> 33:40.602
You even sweet-talked
that soldier from North Korea.

33:41.228 --> 33:43.980
You wiped out the Viper Unit
and became a War Hero.

33:44.898 --> 33:46.691
So why should I have to help you, huh?

33:52.447 --> 33:55.075
I heard you used to work in the mess hall.

33:56.409 --> 33:58.578
I'd like to learn from you,
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

34:04.292 --> 34:05.335
Hey.

34:06.628 --> 34:07.879
Who told you that?

34:09.005 --> 34:10.757
Which bastard was running his mouth?

34:17.847 --> 34:21.142
Warning! Affinity has reached
an all-time low.

34:21.226 --> 34:22.477
Damn it.

34:37.242 --> 34:39.619
Man, you've got it rough.

34:39.911 --> 34:42.789
At this rate, didn't he volunteer
to get out of work?

34:42.872 --> 34:44.916
One who's done it before is worse.

34:45.458 --> 34:47.877
Bread Meal, Bread Meal.

34:47.961 --> 34:49.212
Hey, Tak Mun-ik!

34:50.171 --> 34:51.172
Salute! You're here, sir?

34:51.256 --> 34:53.842
- How can you be eating bread?
- I'm sorry, what was that, sir?

34:53.925 --> 34:55.510
I'm speaking plain as day.

34:55.594 --> 34:57.762
What's there to mishear?

34:57.846 --> 34:58.888
This guy... What the...

35:00.056 --> 35:01.057
What's this?

35:01.349 --> 35:03.059
Where's Kim Kwan-cheol?
Why are you working alone?

35:03.852 --> 35:06.730
- Well, that's...
- That son of a gun Kim Kwan-cheol

35:06.855 --> 35:11.401
I knew something was fishy.
He's just hopeless.

35:12.235 --> 35:14.904
Anyway, our time traveler Tak Mun-ik...

35:14.988 --> 35:15.989
Private First Class Tak Mun-ik!

35:16.072 --> 35:19.701
How did you write the year 1025
on that document?

35:19.784 --> 35:21.202
The year 1025.

35:21.286 --> 35:22.996
Did you come here in a time machine?

35:23.622 --> 35:26.041
- It's not fair, sir!
- Put that down.

35:26.124 --> 35:28.460
Follow me. Let's go back a thousand years.

35:29.461 --> 35:31.963
Master Sergeant!

35:32.047 --> 35:34.549
Headquarters company is in an uproar.
You hear me?

35:35.759 --> 35:38.219
Sergeant Yoon Dong-hyun said
he wasn't this bad.

35:38.303 --> 35:40.472
That's what the Master Sergeant
told me too.

35:40.805 --> 35:43.600
I wonder what happened
to make him change like that.

35:46.728 --> 35:48.104
Yes, Sergeant Major.

35:48.188 --> 35:50.649
It seems one of my guys
made a little mistake.

35:50.732 --> 35:52.275
I'll have it corrected
and sent over right away.

35:52.359 --> 35:53.610
Yes, sir.

35:54.152 --> 35:58.198
Fix it, now. Hey, 1025 was the
Goryeo dynasty, you idiot.

36:00.241 --> 36:02.410
- What is it?
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

36:02.494 --> 36:04.746
It looked like you missed your meal,
so I brought you some food.

36:05.455 --> 36:07.874
Hey, can't you see we're busy here?

36:08.333 --> 36:10.835
Does it look like we have time
to eat right now? Huh?

36:12.045 --> 36:13.046
Take it back...

36:15.298 --> 36:16.299
Take it...

36:16.758 --> 36:18.426
Bring it here. No.

36:19.094 --> 36:20.804
Take it back. Bring it...

36:21.888 --> 36:22.889
Where's the cola?

36:36.277 --> 36:38.613
Well now, look at this.
This guy knows what he's doing.

36:38.697 --> 36:40.824
He even put a perfectly fried egg on top.

36:40.907 --> 36:43.159
The meat is cooked nice and even.

36:45.704 --> 36:47.664
This sauce is the perfect ratio.

36:47.747 --> 36:49.040
The strawberry jam's the real kicker.

36:49.207 --> 36:50.458
You've got taste.

36:50.542 --> 36:52.210
- Hey, Kang Seong-jae.
- Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

36:52.293 --> 36:55.130
So, is Kim Kwan-cheol being helpful?

36:56.005 --> 36:57.006
Huh?

37:02.095 --> 37:03.763
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol...

37:04.681 --> 37:06.433
Yeah, what about him?

37:07.517 --> 37:11.146
I heard he used to be a cook,
and I was curious about that.

37:13.022 --> 37:14.065
That's right.

37:14.733 --> 37:16.276
There was a time like that

37:16.860 --> 37:17.986
for Kim Kwan-cheol.

37:18.945 --> 37:20.196
Come to think of it...

37:20.697 --> 37:23.032
He was a lot like you, Kang Seong-jae.

37:23.658 --> 37:24.659
You know?

37:28.413 --> 37:30.248
So you don't have parents

37:30.331 --> 37:31.624
and you live alone with your grandmother?

37:31.708 --> 37:32.917
Yes, that's right.

37:33.418 --> 37:34.753
What does your grandmother
do for a living?

37:35.211 --> 37:36.713
She sells hamburgers
in front of a university.

37:36.796 --> 37:38.256
I see, fast food.

37:38.339 --> 37:40.175
No. Well, no.

37:41.342 --> 37:43.428
Not fast food,
but old-fashioned hamburger.

37:45.930 --> 37:48.266
Aren't hamburgers fast food?

37:50.018 --> 37:51.019
Isn't it?

37:51.770 --> 37:52.771
No?

37:53.313 --> 37:55.273
Come on, it's the same thing.

37:55.356 --> 37:56.399
Yes, you're right.

37:56.608 --> 37:58.359
Jeez, snap out of it.

37:59.819 --> 38:01.404
Man, this is so frustrating.

38:02.030 --> 38:05.074
Wear this on your chest until
I tell you to take it off.

38:05.366 --> 38:06.367
Got it?

38:07.994 --> 38:10.163
Hey, when someone speaks to you,
answer them!

38:10.246 --> 38:11.247
Yes, sir!

38:15.794 --> 38:17.796
- Kim Kwan-cheol?
- Private Kim Kwan-cheol.

38:17.879 --> 38:20.256
- Do you have any certifications?
- No, I don't.

38:20.340 --> 38:21.549
Okay. You're in.

38:21.633 --> 38:23.218
Congrats. Welcome aboard.

38:24.219 --> 38:26.262
I'll be outside preparing lunch

38:26.346 --> 38:28.890
so you can organize all the
supplies in here.

38:29.182 --> 38:31.476
Private Kim Kwan-cheol.
You mean all of this, sir?

38:32.644 --> 38:34.562
Was I unclear?

38:38.399 --> 38:41.027
Grandma, it's your boy.

38:41.110 --> 38:43.154
Is everything okay, Grandma?

38:44.155 --> 38:45.198
Yeah.

38:45.615 --> 38:46.950
I'm doing fine.

38:48.868 --> 38:49.911
Really, I'm fine.

38:49.994 --> 38:52.080
I told you not to worry about me.

38:52.330 --> 38:53.498
Oh, Grandma.

38:53.581 --> 38:54.833
I'm a cook now.

38:56.751 --> 38:57.752
Isn't that cool?

38:58.753 --> 39:00.380
But being in here...

39:01.589 --> 39:04.759
I'm really craving
the hamburgers you make.

39:06.010 --> 39:07.011
Yeah.

39:07.095 --> 39:08.388
Did you confess to her?

39:08.471 --> 39:10.056
- She got married, sir.
- How old is she?

39:10.139 --> 39:11.683
- She was 35.
- And how old are you?

39:11.766 --> 39:12.851
I'm 22, sir.

39:23.736 --> 39:25.280
- Salute!
- Did you have a good visit?

39:25.363 --> 39:26.489
- Yes, sir.
- Good.

39:26.573 --> 39:29.576
If you're back, gut these anchovies.
What's that in your hand?

39:29.951 --> 39:31.077
Oh, this...

39:31.536 --> 39:34.163
- My grandma gave them to share.
- Huh? What is it?

39:40.753 --> 39:41.754
Hey.

39:44.883 --> 39:46.050
Wow, what kind of burgers are these?

39:46.134 --> 39:48.261
My grandma made these hamburgers herself.

39:48.344 --> 39:49.512
Grandma's cooking is great.

39:49.596 --> 39:51.431
Hey, your grandma

39:51.514 --> 39:53.266
should open a restaurant.

39:53.433 --> 39:54.517
She does.

40:20.460 --> 40:22.712
SESAME SEED HAMBURGER BUN

40:22.795 --> 40:24.255
Hurry up and eat.

40:25.965 --> 40:28.176
You have to eat something
to keep your strength up.

40:31.679 --> 40:33.097
Hey, Kim Kwan-cheol!

40:34.515 --> 40:37.435
You don't think your Master Sergeant's
words matter? Huh?

40:37.518 --> 40:39.187
You punk!

40:39.270 --> 40:42.273
Your grandma would be so proud
to see you like this.

40:43.483 --> 40:44.984
She would still be alive, sir.

40:46.152 --> 40:48.446
If only I hadn't been dragged
into this godforsaken army.

40:52.784 --> 40:54.661
While I was stuck here cooking...

40:57.038 --> 40:58.581
my grandmother...

40:59.248 --> 41:00.667
passed away all alone.

41:04.379 --> 41:05.755
I couldn't even be there
for her in the end...

41:07.173 --> 41:09.217
so how do you expect me
to have an appetite?

41:10.593 --> 41:12.136
Fine. Do whatever you want.

41:20.436 --> 41:23.231
But things don't always go your way
in this world...

41:23.523 --> 41:24.565
kid.

41:41.249 --> 41:42.500
Get up. Get up!

41:42.583 --> 41:44.252
- Get up!
- Where's Kim Kwan-cheol?

41:45.253 --> 41:46.254
Where is he?

41:46.671 --> 41:48.172
Has anyone seen Kim Kwan-cheol?

41:49.465 --> 41:50.466
Kim Kwan-cheol!

41:50.550 --> 41:51.801
- Kwan-cheol!
- Private Kim Kwan-cheol!

41:51.884 --> 41:56.222
- Kwan-cheol! Kim Kwan-cheol!
- Kwan-cheol! Kim Kwan-cheol!

41:56.305 --> 41:59.392
- Kwan-cheol.
- Where did he go? Good grief.

42:13.573 --> 42:15.992
Hey, hey, Kwan-cheol, what are you doing?

42:31.257 --> 42:32.300
Goodness.

42:32.383 --> 42:34.302
What are you doing out here, kid?

42:35.553 --> 42:36.804
Let's get inside. Hurry.

42:37.847 --> 42:38.848
It's cold.

42:43.269 --> 42:44.312
Master Sergeant.

42:47.065 --> 42:48.107
Yeah.

42:51.903 --> 42:53.696
Let's go inside, Kwan-cheol.

42:54.155 --> 42:55.448
Come on, let's go.

42:56.824 --> 42:57.825
Come on.

43:05.917 --> 43:08.294
Honestly. Our Kim Kwan-cheol...

43:08.377 --> 43:11.506
he was the tragic hero
of a real tearjerker.

43:12.965 --> 43:15.426
Yoon Dong-hyun really
had his hands full with him.

43:18.262 --> 43:22.183
- About the hamburger back then, sir.
- Yeah.

43:22.266 --> 43:23.476
Do you happen to remember it?

43:23.559 --> 43:24.685
Yeah.

43:25.061 --> 43:26.938
That thing...

43:27.271 --> 43:29.232
Let's see, what was it...

43:29.524 --> 43:33.611
It wasn't the kind of thing
kids these days would like...

43:33.986 --> 43:34.987
But it...

43:35.613 --> 43:38.533
had the feel of something you'd get
from a small town bakery.

43:39.492 --> 43:41.285
Do you mean it was like a salad sandwich?

43:41.911 --> 43:43.621
No. It wasn't a salad sandwich.

43:44.872 --> 43:46.457
Do you remember what it tasted like?

43:46.833 --> 43:49.502
Well, that thing...

43:52.380 --> 43:53.381
It...

43:55.007 --> 43:56.008
was delicious.

44:14.360 --> 44:15.862
KANG SEONG-JAE

44:26.205 --> 44:28.040
Didn't I tell you not to call me?

44:28.124 --> 44:29.750
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

44:29.834 --> 44:31.669
I called because
I have something to ask you.

44:33.421 --> 44:35.173
This had better be important,
or you're dead.

44:36.966 --> 44:38.843
By any chance...

44:39.302 --> 44:42.471
the hamburger that
Kim Kwan-cheol's grandmother made...

44:42.930 --> 44:43.931
do you remember it?

44:45.558 --> 44:47.643
You called me just to ask that?

44:52.064 --> 44:54.942
Hero, would you like to use a skill?

44:56.861 --> 44:58.446
COMRADE, HELP ME!

45:02.700 --> 45:04.577
It was an old-fashioned hamburger

45:04.660 --> 45:07.496
but it had this savory and sweet taste.

45:07.830 --> 45:10.583
But I have no idea what it was made with.

45:11.250 --> 45:13.044
With "Comrade, help me" skill activated

45:13.127 --> 45:16.005
old-fashioned hamburger recipe
has been acquired.

45:21.761 --> 45:23.179
Yeah, okay.

45:28.184 --> 45:30.269
What am I even saying right now?

45:39.153 --> 45:40.238
OLD-FASHIONED HAMBURGER
SEASON WITH SALT...

45:40.905 --> 45:43.616
After seasoning this and this
with salt and pepper

45:43.699 --> 45:47.662
add breadcrumbs, mix, form a patty,
and on a butter-toasted bun...

45:47.745 --> 45:50.331
spread a mixture of sugar,
mayonnaise, and this.

45:50.414 --> 45:52.750
Add onions prepared like this

45:52.833 --> 45:55.920
and after adding this and this,
top it off with a bun.

46:25.366 --> 46:27.576
Well, it looks the part.

46:33.958 --> 46:34.959
Is it close?

46:39.046 --> 46:40.172
Well, it tastes good.

46:41.757 --> 46:42.925
It's a little off, though.

46:44.218 --> 46:46.262
This isn't it. But it is tasty.

46:56.939 --> 46:57.940
Jeez.

46:59.025 --> 47:00.609
You're really trying hard, aren't you?

47:01.235 --> 47:02.403
Man...

47:03.612 --> 47:04.989
This is good. But this isn't it.

47:06.073 --> 47:07.825
OLD-FASHIONED HAMBURGER
SEASON WITH SALT...

47:07.908 --> 47:10.453
It's a far cry from grandma's cooking.

47:10.536 --> 47:11.537
You can stop now.

47:13.164 --> 47:15.875
CLASS CHANGE QUEST
D-4

47:28.471 --> 47:30.264
SEASON THE GROUND BEEF AND PORK...

47:31.182 --> 47:34.560
After seasoning ground beef and pork
with salt and pepper

47:34.643 --> 47:36.145
add breadcrumbs, mix

47:36.228 --> 47:38.481
form into a patty, and cook.

47:43.402 --> 47:45.112
I told you I don't like hamburgers!

47:45.196 --> 47:47.531
- Please, one bite.
- It's just I was drinking yesterday.

47:47.615 --> 47:49.450
- This is the last one.
- Is this really the last one?

47:49.533 --> 47:50.534
Understood.

47:53.329 --> 47:54.330
Nope.

47:54.413 --> 47:55.414
This isn't the one.

47:56.415 --> 47:58.584
Stop giving me those puppy-dog eyes, jeez.

47:58.667 --> 47:59.877
I said no! Go!

47:59.960 --> 48:02.671
CLASS CHANGE QUEST
D-3

48:06.634 --> 48:10.554
Add a fried egg, ham, and cheese,
then top it off with a bun.

48:18.229 --> 48:19.230
I...

48:20.314 --> 48:21.982
I shouldn't have said anything...

48:22.483 --> 48:23.818
I'm so sorry.

48:25.569 --> 48:27.029
CLASS CHANGE QUEST
D-1

48:27.113 --> 48:28.364
Now...

48:29.782 --> 48:31.534
This is really the last one.

48:32.910 --> 48:34.787
Do you really have to do all this?

48:50.386 --> 48:53.139
It had this savory and sweet flavor.

48:55.224 --> 48:56.892
What kind of sweetness is it?

48:57.977 --> 48:59.687
What kind of sweetness is it?

48:59.770 --> 49:02.815
SAVORY GOLD MAYONNAISE

49:23.752 --> 49:26.130
APPLE JAM

49:43.147 --> 49:44.732
On a toasted bun

49:44.815 --> 49:48.277
spread a mixture of sugar,
mayonnaise, and apple jam.

49:49.028 --> 49:51.113
SPREAD A MIXTURE OF SUGAR,
MAYONNAISE, AND APPLE JAM

49:51.197 --> 49:54.033
ADD ONIONS PREPARED LIKE THIS

49:54.116 --> 49:56.702
It's a far cry from grandma's cooking.

50:27.691 --> 50:31.028
Add caramelized onions.

50:32.029 --> 50:34.657
Oh, so this is caramel... caramelization.

50:40.037 --> 50:41.080
What's this?

50:43.040 --> 50:44.500
Hey, Ace!

50:49.463 --> 50:50.464
Where'd he go?

50:55.094 --> 50:56.136
What is this?

51:07.523 --> 51:08.732
Hey, Kang Seong-jae!

51:10.943 --> 51:14.905
Damn it. All he ever does is stuff
I never asked him to do. Jeez.

53:00.135 --> 53:01.136
Grandma?

53:19.029 --> 53:21.490
Don't cry. There, there.

53:26.537 --> 53:28.580
Don't hate people so much.

53:29.915 --> 53:32.292
It'll all come back to you.

53:33.877 --> 53:34.878
Understand?

53:38.549 --> 53:39.550
Go on, eat up.

53:57.317 --> 53:58.318
Is it good?

54:00.279 --> 54:01.530
It's delicious.

54:46.700 --> 54:47.701
Hey!

54:48.410 --> 54:49.912
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

54:49.995 --> 54:50.996
What are you doing?

54:51.413 --> 54:53.499
You're barely a rookie
and you're already hiding out in here.

54:57.878 --> 55:00.005
I told you I hate
the bread meal, didn't I?

55:00.422 --> 55:01.423
Well...

55:02.758 --> 55:04.676
it can't compare to your grandma's

55:04.760 --> 55:06.512
but I did my best.

55:06.595 --> 55:07.596
Damn it.

55:08.055 --> 55:10.015
There are no secrets in this damn army.

55:13.685 --> 55:15.103
You think this is going
to change anything?

55:16.897 --> 55:18.232
You're ridiculous, seriously.

55:27.199 --> 55:30.410
THOROUGH VIGILANCE AND FLAWLESS MISSIONS

55:43.757 --> 55:44.758
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

55:46.510 --> 55:47.928
What, are you surprised?

55:48.762 --> 55:51.849
I've probably chopped thousands
of cabbages alongside my grandmother.

55:57.604 --> 55:59.439
DISLIKE LEVEL

56:02.359 --> 56:05.529
LIKEABILITY 100%

56:07.281 --> 56:09.491
Quest completed.

56:11.702 --> 56:14.037
A colleague has been added.

56:14.788 --> 56:16.748
Corporal Kim Kwan-cheol.

56:20.043 --> 56:21.837
What are you doing?
If there's more to chop, bring it.

56:23.380 --> 56:24.715
Yes, sir. Thank you.

56:31.346 --> 56:36.476
GANGLIM OUTPOST
(UNIT 2965, 4TH COMPANY)

56:36.560 --> 56:41.398
GANGLIM OUTPOST
(UNIT 2965, 4TH COMPANY)

56:58.832 --> 56:59.917
What the hell?

57:06.089 --> 57:10.469
Typhoon Crow's heading north, bringing
downpours and high winds.

57:10.802 --> 57:13.931
This is an extremely powerful typhoon
with a pressure of 897 hectopascals...

57:14.514 --> 57:15.891
Announcement from the situation room.

57:15.974 --> 57:17.225
All personnel in barracks today...

57:17.309 --> 57:18.352
Hey...

57:18.435 --> 57:20.062
Mic check, one, two, three.

57:20.145 --> 57:22.272
This is Company Commander, Hwang Seok-ho.

57:22.356 --> 57:24.399
Effective immediately,
personnel will aid in repairs.

57:24.483 --> 57:26.860
No exceptions. I want everyone out here.

57:26.944 --> 57:29.571
I just washed up and everything,
and now they're calling us out again?

57:29.655 --> 57:30.656
If it continues on its path north

57:30.739 --> 57:34.242
it's projected to be large enough
to engulf the Korean peninsula.

57:34.326 --> 57:37.663
GANGLIM

57:38.372 --> 57:40.874
Hey, get a move on! What are you doing?

57:40.958 --> 57:43.126
What's with this rain?

57:43.210 --> 57:45.837
At this rate, the outpost
is gonna get washed away!

57:45.921 --> 57:47.547
Oh, for crying out loud!

57:47.631 --> 57:50.759
Hurry up! Faster, faster!

57:50.842 --> 57:52.761
Everything's gonna get washed away,
you hopeless fools!

57:52.844 --> 57:55.555
Get out of the way. I'll do it myself.

57:59.518 --> 58:01.728
All right, move it quickly. Quickly!

58:01.812 --> 58:04.022
- Quickly! Faster, faster!
- And be safe.

58:05.732 --> 58:07.484
Is this really happening?

58:09.277 --> 58:11.947
- Sergeant, the water isn't draining!
- What!

58:12.030 --> 58:13.740
Hey, get out of there.

58:13.824 --> 58:15.867
- Yeah.
- The water's not draining.

58:15.951 --> 58:17.285
You can't do anything without me.

58:17.744 --> 58:18.954
I said dig here!

58:19.037 --> 58:21.540
What are you doing?
Get that rock out of there!

58:21.915 --> 58:25.752
- Can't even handle a shovel...
- Master Sergeant, how long?

58:26.545 --> 58:28.338
Yeah, dig there. Right there.

58:28.422 --> 58:31.008
That, that rock there...

58:31.216 --> 58:32.259
Goodness.

58:32.509 --> 58:34.469
Okay, the wind and rain are getting worse.

58:34.553 --> 58:36.805
Everyone, evacuate to the barracks
for now. Fall back!

58:36.888 --> 58:40.058
Fall back!

58:40.142 --> 58:43.729
- Fall back! Fall back!
- Just go! Hurry up, let's go!

58:43.812 --> 58:45.397
- Fall back!
- Leave it all and go!

58:46.398 --> 58:47.607
Come on, chop-chop.

58:48.608 --> 58:50.110
They said to fall back.

58:50.777 --> 58:52.696
Everyone, move out carefully!

58:54.489 --> 58:56.116
Hurry, let's move!

58:57.951 --> 58:59.494
Oh, my glasses!

59:06.293 --> 59:08.420
- Are you okay?
- Who's there?

59:08.503 --> 59:09.880
Private First Class Kang Seong-jae.

59:09.963 --> 59:12.215
- Kang Seong-jae.
- Yes.

59:12.632 --> 59:15.761
- Move, Kang Seong-jae, Tak Mun-ik!
- Let's go.

59:15.844 --> 59:17.095
Understood.

59:24.895 --> 59:26.730
Kang Seong-jae!

59:28.190 --> 59:29.691
GANGLIM OUTPOST

59:58.929 --> 01:00:01.306
THE LEGEND OF KITCHEN SOLDIER

01:00:03.183 --> 01:00:05.185
- They say the roads are cut off.
- Why isn't this thing working?

01:00:05.268 --> 01:00:07.479
I don't think
we can hold out for much longer.

01:00:08.814 --> 01:00:11.399
What do you mean?
We'll all starve to death together.

01:00:11.566 --> 01:00:14.152
Hey, we can't just sit around
and starve to death.

01:00:14.236 --> 01:00:16.947
Mess Hall Satisfaction Rating
is decreasing.

01:00:19.825 --> 01:00:21.618
Are the soldiers going to burn down
the mess hall?

01:00:22.160 --> 01:00:24.871
- We can't let the soldiers starve.
- Salute!

01:00:24.955 --> 01:00:28.041
- I'll be back.
- We will never be broken.

01:00:28.458 --> 01:00:30.127
I'll keep doing my best.

01:00:30.210 --> 01:00:32.254
And provide you all with delicious meals.
